<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n51443" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθυ-άω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fish, angle</i>, mostly in 
				Ep.
			
			pres. and impf., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθυάασκον γναμπτοῖς ἀγκίστροισιν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.368
				</span></i>
			: c. acc., <i>fish for</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αὐτοῦ δ᾽ ἰχθυάα . . δελφῖνας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.95
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				1.426
			</span></i>:—
				Med.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Lyc.
				46
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>sport</i> (like fish), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δελφῖνες . . ἐθύνεον ἰχθυάοντες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Sc.</u>
					210
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>to be made of fish</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰχθυώμενος ἄρτος</span> (vulg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄργος</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Horap.
				1.14
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
